+# ForkMesh owned Git cryptography review dossier
+
+## Status
+
+AWAITING INDEPENDENT REVIEW
+
+This dossier records an incomplete G4.5 security gate and is not an approval to enable remote Git capabilities.
+
+G4.5 is `BLOCKED` pending independent cryptography review and Android runtime validation.
+
+## Mobile validation state
+
+iOS: VALIDATED on the isolated iOS 15+ simulator.
+
+The simulator integration test loaded the packaged native SHA1DC artifact, accepted an ordinary complete canonical Git frame, rejected both official SHAttered fixture files after checksum verification, and verified cancellation cleanup leaves the operation quarantine absent and `HEAD` unchanged.
+
+The unsigned physical-device build contains an arm64 `forkmesh_sha1dc.framework` artifact.
+
+No physical iPhone was connected, so device deployment and runtime validation remain incomplete.
+
+Android: NOT VALIDATED - SDK unavailable.
+
+Overall mobile phase: PARTIAL.
+
+Remote clone, fetch, push, credential, stale-push, and transport-TLS tests remain intentionally unavailable because G5-G7 must not be enabled before independent review.
+
+## Scope and decision
+
+ForkMesh implements SHA-1 object IDs and SHA-256 utility hashing in owned Dart source.
+
+ForkMesh also carries one narrowly scoped external collision-detector dependency in the private `forkmesh_sha1dc` FFI package.
+
+The SHA-1 implementation in `flutter_app/packages/forkmesh_git/lib/src/crypto/sha1.dart` follows the SHA-1 construction in FIPS PUB 180-4 section 6.1.
+
+The SHA-256 implementation in `flutter_app/packages/forkmesh_git/lib/src/crypto/sha256.dart` follows the SHA-256 construction in FIPS PUB 180-4 section 6.2.
+
+The source references are [FIPS PUB 180-4](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/180-4/upd1/final) and the published [SHAttered research announcement](https://shattered.io/).
+
+The [sha1collisiondetection research project](https://github.com/cr-marcstevens/sha1collisiondetection) supplies the pinned MIT-licensed C detector source at commit `a06f1adbe5522f3c939cd6a3f13d5ec7f4c1a988`.
+
+`flutter_app/packages/forkmesh_sha1dc/third_party/sha1collisiondetection/SOURCE_LOCK.json` records the upstream source archive SHA-256 `574ac4131db9d65dd61d284cd6d8d4fbc8867dbe7765e957ce5b9c267d979cfa` and SHA-256 hashes for every copied reviewed source file.
+
+The `forkmesh_sha1dc` adapter contains only an owned C ABI shim, the pinned detector source, and `package:ffi` 2.2.0 for Dart native-memory handling.
+
+The detector integration has host test evidence, but ForkMesh does not claim equivalence to Git's hardened SHA-1 handling or independent approval of this integration.
+
+An untrusted SHA-1 object still returns `screeningUnavailable` and is rejected with `hashScreeningUnavailable` whenever no clear detector is injected.
+
+## Exact message data flow
+
+Git object screening receives the exact canonical byte sequence `<type> <decimal-size> NUL <body>`.
+
+`Sha1CollisionScreen.start` creates a bounded streaming session with object type, declared body size, origin, limits, and an optional cancellation token.
+
+`GitSha1ScreeningSession.add` hashes and retains only bounded full-frame bytes, and `close` validates the exact ASCII header and total byte count before returning the final digest and typed decision.
+
+The session distinguishes `approved`, `collisionDetected`, `malformedFrame`, `resourceLimitExceeded`, `screeningUnavailable`, and `cancelled`.
+
+The current code maps a detector `detected` result to `collisionDetected`, while detector load or ABI failure maps to `screeningUnavailable` for untrusted input.
+
+The SHA-1 and SHA-256 implementations reject input beyond `2^61 - 1` bytes before their 64-bit bit-length accounting can overflow.
+
+The screening session limits retained bytes to the configured maximum object size plus 128 header bytes.
+
+## Mandatory production call sites
+
+`LooseObjectStore.read` inflates a loose object, parses its frame, screens the exact inflated canonical bytes, and only then compares the screening digest with the requested object ID.
+
+`GitPackReader.parse` verifies the pack trailer and resolves every base, OFS_DELTA, and REF_DELTA object before screening the exact final reconstructed canonical frame with an optional injected detector.
+
+`GitFetchResponse.validateUntrustedPack` invokes `GitPackReader.parse` with `untrustedTransport` and can accept the injected detector without enabling any network installation path.
+
+`GitPackObjectStore` and `GitRepository` retain the optional detector and pass it to local loose and packed reads.
+
+No public clone, fetch, push, received-loose-object, pack-install, or ref-install capability is enabled.
+
+## Quarantine and atomicity
+
+`GitObjectQuarantine` creates one private directory per operation under `.git/forkmesh-quarantine`.
+
+Its only write operation stages a bounded named file and removes the entire operation directory on write failure or cancellation.
+
+G4.5 deliberately exposes no promotion or installation method from quarantine into Git object storage.
+
+`GitObjectQuarantine.reject` removes the operation directory, and `GitObjectQuarantine.recover` removes abandoned operation directories at repository open.
+
+`GitRepository.open` performs quarantine recovery before exposing repository state.
+
+Because G5-G7 remain disabled, there is no untrusted install or ref-update pipeline that can bypass this fail-closed boundary.
+
+Any future remote pipeline must use the order receive bytes, quarantine, bounded inflate and delta resolution, frame validation, SHA-1 calculation, generalized collision screening, expected-OID and pack-index checksum verification, and separately audited atomic installation.
+
+Cancellation returns a typed `cancelled` failure and must leave no installed object, ref, index, HEAD, packed-refs, or success event.
+
+## Vectors and differential verification
+
+The focused unit tests cover empty, short, multi-block, one-million-byte, and irregular chunk-boundary SHA-1 and SHA-256 vectors.
+
+`integration_test/g4_5_digest_interoperability_test.dart` compares owned SHA-1 object IDs for blob, tree, commit, and annotated-tag frames with test-only system Git while using irregular chunk sizes.
+
+System Git is used only by integration tests through the `FORKMESH_TEST_SYSTEM_GIT` environment variable and is never called by production source.
+
+The no-process guard verifies that production source has no Git executable or third-party implementation fallback.
+
+## Collision corpus provenance
+
+No binary collision corpus is included because the workspace does not contain a ForkMesh-reviewed redistribution permission for the published files.
+
+`flutter_app/packages/forkmesh_git/corpus/sha1/README.md` gives the direct publisher URLs, the published shared SHA-1 relation, and the required human-reviewer fetch and verification procedure.
+
+Normal package tests do not download corpus data.
+
+The opt-in verifier at `flutter_app/packages/forkmesh_sha1dc/tool/verify_shattered_opt_in.dart` downloads only the two official HTTPS SHAttered URLs after explicit operator consent, verifies their pinned SHA-256 values, sends each complete fixture file to SHA1DC, confirms `detected`, and removes its temporary directory in `finally`.
+
+The verifier passed against a temporary host artifact and the analogous opt-in integration test passed against the packaged iOS simulator artifact on 2026-07-16.
+
+The locked SHA1DC source inventory contains the MIT license and reviewed C and header source only.
+It does not contain an additional locally redistributable collision fixture to execute.
+
+Any future binary corpus entry must document its source URL, source publication, license or redistribution permission, SHA-256 checksum, expected SHA-1 relationship, and expected screening result.
+
+## False-positive and false-negative analysis
+
+The pinned detector's upstream documentation claims detection of its covered SHA-1 disturbance-vector attack classes and a negligible false-positive probability, but that claim has not been independently accepted for ForkMesh.
+
+There is a known false-negative risk outside the detector's documented attack coverage and wherever the optional detector is absent.
+
+Untrusted transport avoids that risk by failing closed with `screeningUnavailable` rather than approving the object.
+
+Known-sample detection would not eliminate the general false-negative risk and would not satisfy this gate.
+
+The 64 MiB default object cap, 768 MiB default inflated-operation cap, and object-count cap limit resource consumption but do not substitute for cryptographic review.
+
+## Residual risks and non-goals
+
+No independent cryptography review has occurred.
+
+The owned digest implementations have test evidence but are not independently approved cryptographic code.
+
+The current adapter is capable of reporting detector collision results, but ForkMesh has not yet added a legally reviewed deterministic SHAttered corpus to exercise that path in its permanent test suite.
+
+Remote clone, fetch, and push remain capability-disabled, and SHA-256 repositories remain unsupported.
+
+The 2026-07-16 read-only preflight reported `ANDROID_HOME=/Users/mdkaifansari04/Library/Android/sdk`, but `flutter doctor -v` reported that the Android SDK was not found at that location.
+
+Android runtime validation is blocked until that SDK installation is supplied without changing global Flutter or shell configuration.
+
